{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances","id":852652,"title":"What is the narrative role of a Sidereal's Acquintances?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-24T16:30:24-07:00","id":852652,"title":"What is the narrative role of a Sidereal's Acquintances?","content":"So, tinkering with Sidereals, and now I'm pondering- what is the reason to introduce the Acquintances background? What role in a story do Acquintances serve; why do Sidereals cultivate them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T16:40:58-07:00","id":852655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances#post852652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, tinkering with Sidereals, and now I'm pondering- what is the reason to introduce the Acquintances background? What role in a story do Acquintances serve; why do Sidereals cultivate them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are people who remember the Sidereal and that the Sidereal can have an actual Human Relationship with without lies or Resplendent Destinies. They are the Sidereal's touch stone with their humanity. Acquaintances (or lack there of) are the most important part of a Sidereal's backstory.<br /> <br /> The Ex2 Sidereal book never really got into how a Sidereal forms social connections with Acquaintances. There is that one Ride Charm, Breaking the Wild Mortal, but it only lasts for one story. I just head canon it that the Sidereal must spend time and effort visiting and spending time with the person. After the Sidereal has broken though Arcane Fate, they must regularly visit the social group to maintain that connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-24-2016, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T16:48:06-07:00","id":852661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852655#post852655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are people who remember the Sidereal and that the Sidereal can have an actual Human Relationship with without lies or Resplendent Destinies. They are the Sidereal's touch stone with their humanity. Acquaintances (or lack there of) are the most important part of a Sidereal's backstory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just... hrm.<br /> Who are some examples of acquintances from various bits of source material?<br /> The only one that comes to mind even remotely are like, the supporting cast of various costumed super hero types (Alfred, Foggy, some iterations of Lois)- and even they don't exactly fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T16:56:22-07:00","id":852665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852661#post852661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just... hrm.<br /> Who are some examples of acquintances from various bits of source material?<br /> The only one that comes to mind even remotely are like, the supporting cast of various costumed super hero types (Alfred, Foggy, some iterations of Lois)- and even they don't exactly fit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are not really any canon examples. That one comic with May Blossom could be interpreted as her trying to develop the Clerk boy into an Acquaintance.<br /> <br /> Alfred is more like a Follower or Ally. Acquaintances are more like Hawkeye's Family in Age of Ultron, or Aunt May in Spiderman, or Vash's Skyship friends in Trigun. (I'll try to think of more examples.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T17:01:49-07:00","id":852672,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any good examples of using them in a game.<br /> <br /> I feel what's missing most from Acquaintances is <i>leverage</i>. With Allies, Contacts, Spies, Retainers, etc., you either have important people who can help you, or an information network, or people who can I guess handle mundane tasks when you're around.<br /> <br /> Yeah, let's add Retainers to this. Acquaintances and Retainers feel sort of like pure story fodder with no tangible benefit. Why do they have an associated cost? Practically, what are they good for? I get the story/narrative element to them but not the actual gaming/mechanical element. I'm not sold on them being things you should have to pay build resources for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T17:03:23-07:00","id":852675,"title":"","content":"Basically, I'm wondering if 'Acquaintance' is really just 'Anyone who has an enduring positive intimacy towards the Sidereal'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T17:07:11-07:00","id":852680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852672#post852672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have any good examples of using them in a game.<br /> <br /> I feel what's missing most from Acquaintances is <i>leverage</i>. With Allies, Contacts, Spies, Retainers, etc., you either have important people who can help you, or an information network, or people who can I guess handle mundane tasks when you're around.<br /> <br /> Yeah, let's add Retainers to this. Acquaintances and Retainers feel sort of like pure story fodder with no tangible benefit. Why do they have an associated cost? Practically, what are they good for? I get the story/narrative element to them but not the actual gaming/mechanical element. I'm not sold on them being things you should have to pay build resources for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll agree that it's kind of bullshit that my character has to spend three background points and one bonus point to have any sort of meaningful relationship with a mortal, be it romantic or platonic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T17:23:33-07:00","id":852692,"title":"","content":"honestly, this part of Sidereals doesn't seem to be inspired by anything in particular. I doubt you could find any examples in all of media, except in a metaphorical rather than literal sense. A secret agent having relationships outside their job is the closest you could probably come to it: sure the secret agent (and we're talking like, fictional super-spy kind of secret agent) is incredibly competent and goes to places all over the world, kicks ass and makes sure bad things do not happen or accomplishes some other mission, but all that is still their JOB, what they do for a living, not them actually living, and work can stress you so you need something non-work related, and Acquaintances are like, the secret agents friends who don't even know what their job is and are just people they hang out with because man, being a secret agent requires you to lie, and be in disguise and work with demanding superiors who expect you to fix everyone's problems with your spy-ness,and sometimes you just got to get away from that, especially when your job involves ending the lives of people whether they deserve it or not, making sure certain secrets are kept so that they come out at a certain time and probably cause a lot of pain and suffering like whether or not someone's husband is cheating on somebody, causing battles to happen, or making people go on journeys across Creation which is full of dangers to survive.<br /> <br /> and Sidereals have it hard, because their non-spy friends could forget them if they don't maintain relationships. I doubt there is anything that particularly matches aside from other WW stuff involving secret conspiracies or whatever.<br /> <br /> but yeah, Acquaintances are basically the Sidereals &quot;people that aren't involved with your job that know you&quot; background, because imagine you get kidnapped to a continent sized city where you've been chosen to work 24-7 with a bunch of people whose jobs it is to make sure reality works right, and every single person there is a part of that job in some way, and your trained your entire rest of life there to eventually become your own agent, so that you work for 5000 years more there, and every single person there is playing politics in some way and all the humans you know there are scheming masterminds who are searching for every single bit of advantage they can get while not insulting the people they work with all for the sake of making sure everything runs smoothly and nothing goes wrong and reality works right, and that your expected to somehow carry on the job when the world is the worst it has ever been and all the people outside the city whose job it is to make sure reality works right are all corrupt mafias who are being attacked by the police your predecessors set up but that said police is currently starting to divide and fight itself....<br /> <br /> yeah, wouldn't YOU find some way to escape all that for a bit? y'know just a break from that headache you get when the Dragon-Blooded go after the wrong thing, or when a Solar thwarts you carefully laid plans again, or when the Fair Folk suddenly decide to have fun with the next door nation while your trying to figure out what these Yozi cultists are up to, or when the freaking Empress goes missing and all the Houses are now focusing one each other rather than the new influx of Solars all of a sudden, or when two gods can't stop arguing about what the weather should be like today while the plant gods make all the crops die just as a form of protest until they can make up their mind thus causing all the mortals to start getting angry and raiding other people for food...its all a complicated pain. when sometimes what you need is just some simple relaxation with people you can talk to without needing to manipulate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T17:35:01-07:00","id":852695,"title":"","content":"Acquaintances are like the people at Cheers if Norm was the Sidereal. It's a place where everyone knows the Sidereal's name and where the Sidereal can just chill and have a beer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T17:48:42-07:00","id":852701,"title":"","content":"It's also a pull from OWoD Mage, which the Sids were tenuously linked to in 1e, like all the major Exalted splats kind of linked to an OWoD splat.<br /> <br /> Arcane Fate is the equivalent to the Arcane background in Mage, where people basically forget you. The higher the rating, the quicker they forget and the &quot;worse&quot; it is, i.e., I don't think someone whose wife had Arcane 1 would forget her, but with Arcane 5, that's going to happen sooner or later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852675#post852675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, I'm wondering if 'Acquaintance' is really just 'Anyone who has an enduring positive intimacy towards the Sidereal'</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly a better way of handling it than requiring build points be devoted to having friends who remember you.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852692#post852692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">especially when your job involves ending the lives of people whether they deserve it or not, making sure certain secrets are kept so that they come out at a certain time and probably cause a lot of pain and suffering like whether or not someone's husband is cheating on somebody, causing battles to happen, or making people go on journeys across Creation which is full of dangers to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's be real here too: it's not like the Sids' jobs actually makes sense or has ever really been explained in a sensical reasons beyond &quot;Fate gonna Fate, Maidens gonna be secretive.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 03-24-2016, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:16:19-07:00","id":852712,"title":"","content":"I've never considered it before but... would the Scarlet Empress be an Acquaintance to Chejop Kejak? It would make sense for her to be... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">let's add Retainers to this.</div> </div> </div> </div> What, from World of Darkness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:35:21-07:00","id":852726,"title":"","content":"My impression is that making Acquaintances a background was meant to say that your connections to the mortal world were rare enough to be a precious commodity even for a god-king who lives in undreamed-of splendour -- to emphasize the lonely separation of the role and encourage you to value the connections you had, and to show an ironic contrast between the glories of Heaven and the humble pleasures of ordinary life. In practice, I'm not sure how well this worked. I think they needed an appropriate-feeling mechanical benefit or some Charm hooks that didn't involve sacrificing them for the greater good, because you're not likely to be RPing scenes with your acquaintances often in-play, and so not taking any &quot;feels&quot; like you're just playing the exact same character but with more background dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:40:45-07:00","id":852729,"title":"","content":"What is the &quot;mechanical benefit&quot; of Allies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:41:54-07:00","id":852730,"title":"","content":"Hm. Maybe they could tie into their Limit mechanic? Spending time immersed in mundanity with your Acquintances helps to reduce the stress and strain of your super-spy life, etcetc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:41:59-07:00","id":852731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852680#post852680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll agree that it's kind of bullshit that my character has to spend three background points and one bonus point to have any sort of meaningful relationship with a mortal, be it romantic or platonic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the curse of being a Sidereal. Blame Chejop Kejak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:44:27-07:00","id":852733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852729#post852729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the &quot;mechanical benefit&quot; of Allies?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You have a badass friend that is generally willing to help you out.<br /> A three dot ally is a young Terrestrial; a five dot ally is a Celestial Exalt or thereabouts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:53:41-07:00","id":852737,"title":"","content":"Those aren't mechanical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:54:21-07:00","id":852738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852730#post852730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Maybe they could tie into their Limit mechanic? Spending time immersed in mundanity with your Acquintances helps to reduce the stress and strain of your super-spy life, etcetc?</div> </div> </div> </div>This would make sense I think, depending on how Sidereal limit works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T19:02:37-07:00","id":852744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852729#post852729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the &quot;mechanical benefit&quot; of Allies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Allies tend to be willing and able to do things for you that have very substantial in-game benefits. Acquaintances are the opposite of that -- they're generally &quot;little people&quot; who can't do anything much for you except assist with your mental health. That's the kind of thing that really requires a mechanical hook to be reified in the context of a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T19:03:07-07:00","id":852746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852729#post852729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the &quot;mechanical benefit&quot; of Allies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having an Ally who could come to your aid/lend succor in some sphere or another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852737#post852737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those aren't mechanical.</div> </div> </div> </div>what<br /> <br /> It certainly can be.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 03-24-2016, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T19:04:39-07:00","id":852747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852737#post852737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those aren't mechanical.</div> </div> </div> </div>I- what?<br /> <br /> They aren't mechanical, in the sense that they don't add dice to a roll.<br /> <br /> They are story driving, however, in that they can be leveraged by characters to aid in resolving problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T19:50:02-07:00","id":852763,"title":"","content":"I think it's useful for Sidereals to cultivate a network of assets, contacts and resources that know nothing about the workings of the Celestial Bureaucracy, and that can be used to operate under the veil of plausible deniability, or who can act in ways that won't draw attention to Heaven or the Fivescore Fellowship. Sometimes, you need to assassinate an Abyssal without letting anyone know who's responsible. <br /> <br /> That depends a lot on whether or not you want to push the spy aspect of the Sidereals though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T03:32:54-07:00","id":852876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852672#post852672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, let's add Retainers to this. Acquaintances and Retainers feel sort of like pure story fodder with no tangible benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>A four dot Retainer can be a yound DB - same as a 3-dot Ally, but much more loyal to you. How is it not a tangible benefit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T04:30:15-07:00","id":852887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852763#post852763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's useful for Sidereals to cultivate a network of assets, contacts and resources that know nothing about the workings of the Celestial Bureaucracy, and that can be used to operate under the veil of plausible deniability, or who can act in ways that won't draw attention to Heaven or the Fivescore Fellowship. Sometimes, you need to assassinate an Abyssal without letting anyone know who's responsible.<br /> <br /> That depends a lot on whether or not you want to push the spy aspect of the Sidereals though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like it's covered by Allies and Retainers though. Acquintances emphasize, repeatedly, that they're just regular folk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T06:04:44-07:00","id":852916,"title":"","content":"I think that, as has already been mentioned, the Acquaintances are designed with the idea that they are people with whom a Sidereal can just relax and be themselves - they're mortals, and thus unlikely to have any agendas with regards to Heavenly politics, they're normal folks, so they don't have much when it comes to mortal politics (necessarily), and the Sidereals can build relationships with them.<br /> <br /> They are there to humanize the Sidereals, to remind them what it is like to live in Creation. To a Bronze Sidereal, they might be a representation of why it is so important to ensure that Solars do not get control of the world again - mortals like their friends were slain in great numbers when the Solars went mad. To a Gold, they are reminders of why it is important to have the Solars in charge again - because their friends' lives <i>suck</i>, and the Solars made things better. To an Independent, it may simply be a deep connection as to why it is important to continue doing their job - the regulation of Fate makes the lives of others like their friends less likely to end because of reasons (whatever those may be).<br /> <br /> Acquaintances are the mundane friends of a Sidereal - outside the Heavenly politics of Yu-Shan or the Bureaucratic rivalries of their fellows, these are people to whom the Sidereal can show their true face, and just complain about how crappy their job is, or the like, over tea or alcohol, without fear that their superiors will hear and offer them some sort of punishment. The life of a Sidereal is full of incredible tension even as it's a series of mundane bureaucratic jobs - is that god trying to force you into showing off your opinion on a matter that will harm the interests of your Bureau? Is this being a spy for Rakan Thulio, or is he just addicted to Celestial Cocaine and trying to get his next hit? Etc. Acquaintances are those with whom the Sidereal can forget about such things and just... be themselves. <br /> <br /> Whether this is something that they should be charged bonus points for is another question, but it seems a premature one to me, given how in 3e the exact nature of Sidereal Arcane Fate is not clear, and whether Acquaintances will be making a return as a merit is unknown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T06:15:41-07:00","id":852923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852672#post852672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, let's add Retainers to this. Acquaintances and Retainers feel sort of like pure story fodder with no tangible benefit. Why do they have an associated cost? Practically, what are they good for? I get the story/narrative element to them but not the actual gaming/mechanical element. I'm not sold on them being things you should have to pay build resources for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the Retainers Merit? It gives you a loyal servant with a 4 or 5 in their main skill, which might be anything from Presence to Melee to Craft, and that's just the 2-dot version.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T06:23:23-07:00","id":852924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>*End</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852916#post852916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether this is something that they should be charged bonus points for is another question, but it seems a premature one to me, given how in 3e the exact nature of Sidereal Arcane Fate is not clear, and whether Acquaintances will be making a return as a merit is unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it matters to me at the moment insofar as I'm tinkering with Sidereals, and several of their prior Charms deal with acquiring Acquintances, or turning them into riding dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T06:27:14-07:00","id":852927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852923#post852923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you read the Retainers Merit? It gives you a loyal servant with a 4 or 5 in their main skill, which might be anything from Presence to Melee to Craft, and that's just the 2-dot version.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I don't read the rules I just complain<br /> <br /> Actually since we were talking about Acquaintences I was thinking of the 2 version of stuff like it and Henchmen and forgot that Retainers was in the 3e core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T06:56:16-07:00","id":852942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852927#post852927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually since we were talking about Acquaintences I was thinking of the 2 version of stuff like it and Henchmen and forgot that Retainers was in the 3e core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I figured.<br /> <br /> I recall Henchmen/Retainers being pretty good though. Weren't they something like &quot;<i>x</i> heroic mortals that serve you for Reasons?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T07:02:02-07:00","id":852944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852887#post852887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems like it's covered by Allies and Retainers though. Acquintances emphasize, repeatedly, that they're just regular folk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regular folks are who I'm talking about. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T07:40:18-07:00","id":852966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=852944#post852944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regular folks are who I'm talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you assassinate an Abyssal with regular folk? Ones who barely remember you when you're not around, no less?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T07:43:57-07:00","id":852969,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think there are whole lot of stories where the character is a complete cipher and have a coterie of otherwise unuseful ordinary people who aren't engaged in their secret world who they have connections with. Except those in which those people are their family / vulnerability. Otherwise, you know, they only really have contact with other specialists. (This is mostly because most stories, wisely, do not go down the route of Sidereal angst about being alienated from the mortal world, and those that do, know it's generally more fun for the hero to get a skilled or powerful friend to break his isolation than an ordinary one).<br /> <br /> If Acquaintances were kept, it might make sense to reverse it to be Intensive Training or something, where you pick dots of it to model the fact that you're like Ahn Aru and have trained too intensely to have any time for picking up any kind of social connections. Unless that's a &quot;bonus points for Flaws&quot; type practice that we want to discourage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T08:28:53-07:00","id":852982,"title":"","content":"Is it getting into too much thread drift to ask whether Exalted's themes and institutions even translate very well to the spy-story stuff that seems to be the most interesting part of Sids' jobs? I mean, this seems to be at least part of the reason for Acquaintances, saying that your job is your life and nobody remembers you except these couple of people? Though thankfully stuff like &quot;break this wagon spoke so a guy eats fish instead of mutton and chokes on a tiny bone&quot; and &quot;kill this baby to show you're impartial&quot; won't be making a reappearance. They just never struck me as being particularly...Exalted kinds of story or conflict.<br /> <br /> I don't think spy games when I think Exalted, even Sidereals. I think NWoD Demon, among other systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T08:39:21-07:00","id":852989,"title":"","content":"Men in Black has something similar going on, though I don't know of any instance of someone remembering A Thing after being flashed.<br /> <br /> I think they exist to highlight the loneliness of operating under the broken mask; for those moments where <i>someone actually remembers you!</i>, but it's a memory that's fragile and fleeting and will fade if you don't kindle it and keep it going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:22:51-07:00","id":853011,"title":"","content":"My personal inspiration of Sidereals includes Investigators, Auditors, and Fixers in addition to Spies. You are an impartial (maybe) outsider coming into a situation and fix it. Having a cover may make your job easier, but you don't have to go all James Bond about it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Traveller_in_Black\" target=\"_blank\">The Traveller in Black</a> is the recommended inspiration from the developers for Sidereals and their place as bringers of order to Chaos.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Watch_(Lukyanenko_novel)\" target=\"_blank\">Sergei Lukyanenko's Night Watch </a>captures the Bureaucratic side of Sidereals really well.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://aliettedebodard.com/bibliography/novels/obsidian-and-blood/\" target=\"_blank\">Aliette de Bodard's Obsidian and Blood</a> is a good example of a Sidereal investigating gods gone bad.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://pern.wikia.com/wiki/Harper\" target=\"_blank\">The Harpers</a> in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragonriders_of_Pern\" target=\"_blank\">Anne McCaffrey's Dragonriders of Pern</a> are Chosen of Serenity who act as advisers and information gatherers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-25-2016, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:36:52-07:00","id":853024,"title":"","content":"I always saw Acquaintances lack of utility as deliberate. It's there to remind you that you can't just make friends like a normal person. If you look at a bunch of normal folks who are genuinely friendly to you and say &quot;that's not worth bonus points, it doesn't give me any mechanical benefits,&quot; well, that's part of the test.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:38:26-07:00","id":853025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=853011#post853011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal inspiration of Sidereals includes Investigators, Auditors, and Fixers in addition to Spies. You are an impartial (maybe) outsider coming into a situation and fix it. Having a cover may make your job easier, but you don't have to go all James Bond about it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Traveller_in_Black\" target=\"_blank\">The Traveller in Black</a> is the recommended inspiration from the developers for Sidereals and their place as bringers of order to Chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oooh, I am unfamiliar with the Traveller in Black, but that seems a thing to rectify!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:45:50-07:00","id":853030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=853025#post853025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oooh, I am unfamiliar with the Traveller in Black, but that seems a thing to rectify!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just read it a couple of months ago. It takes a bit to get into, but give it a chance. It is an awesome book. And it's only 2 bucks on <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B00J5X5OM2/ref=dp-kindle-redirect?ie=UTF8&amp;btkr=1\" target=\"_blank\">Kindle</a>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:54:28-07:00","id":853034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=853024#post853024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always saw Acquaintances lack of utility as deliberate. It's there to remind you that you can't just make friends like a normal person. If you look at a bunch of normal folks who are genuinely friendly to you and say &quot;that's not worth bonus points, it doesn't give me any mechanical benefits,&quot; well, that's part of the test.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My big issue with buying Acquaintances is that to have a relationship with an Individual, not just a group, you need to have Acquaintances 4. In my personal experience, RPing with a nebulous group of NPCs is not as satisfying as a single NPC with a strong backstory. The result is that any Acquaintance background under 3 is not likely to come up in game, but that may just be my experience as an ST and a player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T10:10:46-07:00","id":853044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=853024#post853024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always saw Acquaintances lack of utility as deliberate. It's there to remind you that you can't just make friends like a normal person. If you look at a bunch of normal folks who are genuinely friendly to you and say &quot;that's not worth bonus points, it doesn't give me any mechanical benefits,&quot; well, that's part of the test.</div> </div> </div> </div>This issue is forcing crunch solutions to particular narrative problems. I wouldn't call this good design even if it was deliberate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:05:53-07:00","id":853064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=853024#post853024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always saw Acquaintances lack of utility as deliberate. It's there to remind you that you can't just make friends like a normal person. If you look at a bunch of normal folks who are genuinely friendly to you and say &quot;that's not worth bonus points, it doesn't give me any mechanical benefits,&quot; well, that's part of the test.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with this is that it doesn't really have any effect on the game. Unless the GM goes out of their way to play this up all the time (which is, in essence, a way of making sure the people who took Acquaintances get their &quot;money's worth&quot;), the character with a couple dots of Acquaintances <i>feels </i>identical to the character with none to both the player and the group. This is because Acquaintances are set up in such a way that they and the role they serve in your life are almost entirely outside the sweep of the game's &quot;camera&quot;. You are not going to be roleplaying a scene where you just chill out and have a normal one-on-one conversation with That One Trader Who Lives Near Chiaroscuro, so the fact that your life is devoid of such commonplaces doesn't register emotionally.<br /> <br /> In theory, Acquaintances have some conceptual overlap with Contacts, which are otherwise unavailable to Sidereals, but in practice they have such vastly superior methods of achieving the same thing, and work over such a broad area, that you will likely get at most a single scene in the entire campaign where you drop into the local theatre you own with your friends, ask about what's going on locally with such-and-such, and then breeze off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:22:55-07:00","id":853073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=853064#post853064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are not going to be roleplaying a scene where you just chill out and have a normal one-on-one conversation with That One Trader Who Lives Near Chiaroscuro, so the fact that your life is devoid of such commonplaces doesn't register emotionally.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true.<br /> Maybe if those Resplendent Destiny effects that allowed you to crash at someone's place worked exclucively on Acquaintances? ... nah, that's not great.<br /> <br /> I feel like there's some salvageable mechanics-as-metaphor going on with it, but as it is it's like a Background that's only there for world-building and not to actually be <i>taken</i>. Which is probably fine, its presence still makes a statement: &quot;this is how Sidereals keep mortal &quot;friends&quot;. And it's shitty, and it's hard.&quot;<br /> <br /> Presumably 3e will just make it a Story Merit and people can just get it for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 03-25-2016, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T12:43:43-07:00","id":853118,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3950_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3950\" data-vbnamecard=\"3950\">wonderandawe</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar104_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"104\" data-vbnamecard=\"104\">Gayo</a>, I think you're right, it won't tend to come up. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar43_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"43\" data-vbnamecard=\"43\">Fata-Ku</a> says, I don't think it's really meant for you to spend points on, given a pretty unreasonable price on something of nebulous value and low replacement cost (you can whip up more with a Charm if you wanted).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3420_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3420\" data-vbnamecard=\"3420\">Zelbinnean</a> I don't think it's an issue of crunch <i>solving</i> a fluff <i>problem. </i>Rather, it's unfair crunch reflecting an unfair reality. Defying the broken Mask is as hard as, say, getting your hands on an Artifact, and no, it doesn't give you the same material benefits. I think it's more fair to say it's a fluff paragraph masquerading as a crunch paragraph. I'm not trying to defend the design, exactly, but I don't think it was an accident either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T13:03:27-07:00","id":853135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=853011#post853011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Traveller_in_Black\" target=\"_blank\">The Traveller in Black</a> is the recommended inspiration from the developers for Sidereals and their place as bringers of order to Chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Traveller in Black gives us our the sense of them as rather difficult to know &quot;Odinic wanderers&quot; bringing order to chaos by cleverness and trickery.<br /> <br /> Great Work of Time is what you want to get the grandeur and tragedy of the Sidereals - the scale of the changes they are supposed to achieve, what they are supposed to prevent and the risks of its own that imposes on the world. Which often doesn't come across so much, in much discussion about the Sidereals. (Reading the novella at a fairly impressionable age is probably part of why Sidereals click well for me, as &quot;Obviously they're the heroes&quot;). I hope the 3e team really try and communicate that sense that you get from GWoT, that they are doing things which are impactful to the world, have clear reasons, has sympathetic power, and yet have questionable consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T13:07:59-07:00","id":853137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=853135#post853135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great Work of Time is what you want to get the grandeur and tragedy of the Sidereals - the scale of the changes they are supposed to achieve, what they are supposed to prevent and the risks of its own that imposes on the world. Which often doesn't come across so much, in much discussion about the Sidereals. (Reading the novella at a fairly impressionable age is probably part of why Sidereals click well for me, as &quot;Obviously they're the heroes&quot;). I hope the 3e team really try and communicate that sense that you get from GWoT, that they are doing things which are impactful to the world, have clear reasons, has sympathetic power, and yet have questionable consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Great-Work-Time-John-Crowley-ebook/dp/B00DUXY8D4/ref=sr_1_1_twi_kin_1?s=books&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1458936293&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Great+Work+of+Time\" target=\"_blank\">This book? <br /> </a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T13:11:36-07:00","id":853139,"title":"","content":"Yep!........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T13:13:20-07:00","id":853140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/852652-what-is-the-narrative-role-of-a-sidereal-s-acquintances?p=853139#post853139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep!........</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Damn! I was hoping you'd say &quot;No, it's this other book readily available on Kindle!&quot; lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","val